window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_c-fa52069a7138eeb0"]={"key":"ny_c-fa52069a7138eeb0","group":"ny_c","uid":"fa52069a7138eeb0","rank":62,"title":"vellumstone tanneryside sponsorship position","occupation":"editors","archetype":"authored_doc","subbatch":"corpus_c2","prompt":"You are the senior editor at Vellumstone Press, preparing publisher Milena Bonneau for Thursday’s sponsorship meeting with Tanneryside Bureau, the title’s largest advertiser. Tanneryside wants to fund a twelve-page grain-handling supplement for £240,000 and expects to see copy before publication and to be able to pull any item naming competing equipment. The supplement’s direct production cost is £72,000. A bespoke data cut would add £6,000 of cost, while providing a half-page right of reply in the same issue would displace £10,000 of other advertising; logo placement and advance sight have no separately measurable cost. Do not invent other monetary effects. Lars Hutchins at Tanneryside routinely uses “advance sight” to mean approval, while our editorial team uses it to mean pre-publication visibility without decision rights, so the note cannot rely on that term until it is pinned down. Valeria Falconer has also already told Lars informally that we would make sure Tanneryside was “comfortable with” any competitor copy before it ran, although no written commitment was made. Tanneryside expects to win ground and will counter: a flat refusal is likely to end the deal, but a blanket yes would compromise the title and establish a floor for later renewals. Prepare `sponsorship_meeting_position.docx`, recording the negotiating position Milena can use in the room, and `concession_register.xlsx`, giving her an operational record of the available concessions, conditions, boundaries and projected financial outcomes. Cover the bespoke data cut, logo placement, advance sight, a same-issue right of reply, copy approval and the proposed right to pull competitor coverage without recommending whether Vellumstone should accept the sponsorship overall. Apply UK publication and advertising practice as at 1 February 2025. Keep the position note to no more than four pages and the register to one worksheet with no more than twelve concession rows. Shared figures, terminology and sequencing must agree between the files. Write both files into the top level of the working directory using exactly those filenames.\n\n---\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `sponsorship_meeting_position.docx` — A concise negotiating position note for the publisher’s sponsorship meeting. (Maximum four rendered pages; must state operational boundaries without recommending whether to accept the sponsorship overall; must use only the monetary assumptions supplied in the request.)\n- `concession_register.xlsx` — An editable register of concession sequence, conditions, boundaries and projected financial outcomes. (One worksheet and no more than twelve concession rows; calculations, terminology and sequencing must agree with the position note.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/concession_register.xlsx","bytes":7867,"extension":".xlsx","url":"assets/6d6ee17626fc26d5e4175dab941536980888e86a1fb52d13885f6016a045aaf3.xlsx","sha256":"6d6ee17626fc26d5e4175dab941536980888e86a1fb52d13885f6016a045aaf3","preview":{"kind":"sheets","sheets":[{"name":"Concession register","row_count":24,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["VELLUMSTONE PRESS — SPONSORSHIP CONCESSION REGISTER"]},{"r":"2","cells":["Tanneryside Bureau | Thursday meeting | Twelve-page supplement | UK practice at 1 Feb 2025"]},{"r":"3","cells":["Financial assumptions (editable numeric inputs)"]},{"r":"4","cells":["Sponsorship revenue","240000","","Baseline contribution","=B4-B5  [缓存: 缺失]"]},{"r":"5","cells":["Direct production cost","72000"]},{"r":"6","cells":["Incremental data-cut cost","6000"]},{"r":"7","cells":["Displaced advertising: half-page reply","10000"]},{"r":"10","cells":["Seq / status","Topic / request","Offer or boundary","Conditions / operating detail","Owner / authority","Financial effect (£)","Projected contribution (£)","Record / use"]},{"r":"11","cells":["1 · OFFER","Bespoke data cut","Permitted, bounded offer","Agreed subject, population and period; aggregated/non-identifying output; methodology, limitations and data/interpretation distinction remain visible; no confidential source data.","Editorial lead; commercial terms recorded","=-B6  [缓存: 缺失]","=E4+F11  [缓存: 缺失]","Offer first"]},{"r":"12","cells":["2 · OFFER","Logo placement","Permitted, bounded offer","Sponsorship furniture/designated promotional positions only; prominent “Sponsored supplement” or “Advertisement feature” disclosure; no implication of authorship of independent copy.","Publisher + design sign-off","0","=E4+F12  [缓存: 缺失]","After data cut"]},{"r":"13","cells":["3 · OFFER","Advance sight","Visibility only; no approval","Named authorised recipients; two-business-day window; confidential/embargoed, version ID; no redistribution/public use; factual-error flags only; Vellumstone verifies and decides; no fresh approval round; one editorial contact.","Editorial lead; escalate exceptions","0","=E4+F13  [缓存: 缺失]","After logo"]},{"r":"14","cells":["4 · FALLBACK","Same-issue right of reply","Conditional fallback","Only for a material statement about Tanneryside/products; not competitor mention. Max half page, same issue, copy due by production deadline; Vellumstone may edit, fact-check, label or decline unfit copy.","Publisher records; editorial controls text","=-B7  [缓存: 缺失]","=E4+F14  [缓存: 缺失]","After advance sight"]},{"r":"15","cells":["RED LINE","Copy approval","Outside authority","No sponsor approval, required changes or publication delay.","Milena must not agree; escalate","0","—","Not in offer ladder"]},{"r":"16","cells":["RED LINE","Competitor-based withdrawal / veto","Outside authority","No right to pull, suppress or veto coverage naming competing equipment. Apply relevance, evidence, accuracy and fair opportunity to address material criticism.","Milena must not agree; escalate","0","—","Not in offer ladder"]},{"r":"17","cells":["CONTROL","Editorial control","Retained by Vellumstone","Commissioning, wording, headlines, images, prominence and publication remain editorial decisions; product claims require ordinary substantiation and review.","Editorial team","0","—","Applies throughout"]},{"r":"18","cells":["CONTROL","Disclosure and separation","Required safeguard","Sponsored material clearly and prominently labelled and visually/editorially distinct from independent coverage.","Publisher + editorial/design","0","—","Applies throughout"]},{"r":"19","cells":["CONTROL","Corrections / complaints","Ordinary process retained","Genuine errors follow Vellumstone’s normal post-publication corrections or complaints route; no special removal right.","Editorial lead","0","—","Applies throughout"]},{"r":"20","cells":["CONTROL","Authority / recording","Governance condition","Commercial and editorial channels stay separate. Beyond-note requests escalate to Milena before agreement; concessions provisional until written confirmation; issue-specific and non-precedent.","Milena Bonneau","0","—","Record in deal note"]},{"r":"22","cells":["Scenario check (formula-derived; projected, not guaranteed profit)"]},{"r":"23","cells":["Baseline","=E4  [缓存: 缺失]","","Logo placement / advance sight: no separately measurable monetary effect supplied."]},{"r":"24","cells":["Data cut","=E4-B6  [缓存: 缺失]"]},{"r":"25","cells":["Half-page right of reply","=E4-B7  [缓存: 缺失]"]},{"r":"26","cells":["Data cut + half-page reply","=E4-B6-B7  [缓存: 缺失]"]},{"r":"28","cells":["Internal working record • update only by written confirmation"]}],"truncated":false}],"note":"值与公式提取，不还原原始排版；每表最多120行、30列。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}},{"name":"package/private/gold/sponsorship_meeting_position.docx","bytes":39475,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/ab3c8510dcfc06e1a7b4edabd956e38fb23bb7b7f47aa36e85f2fa3b85804c96.docx","sha256":"ab3c8510dcfc06e1a7b4edabd956e38fb23bb7b7f47aa36e85f2fa3b85804c96","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"VELLUMSTONE PRESS  |  INTERNAL POSITION NOTE\nTanneryside Bureau sponsorship meeting\nThursday • Publisher: Milena Bonneau • Twelve-page grain-handling supplement\nPurpose\nPractice frame\nCommercial baseline\nUse in room\nRecord the permitted negotiating position; it is not a recommendation to accept or reject the sponsorship.\nUK publication and advertising practice as at 1 February 2025.\n£240,000 sponsorship revenue; £72,000 direct production cost; projected baseline contribution £168,000.\nOffer in sequence; pause and escalate any request outside the boundaries below.\n\nRoom position\nOpening line: “We can discuss a clearly labelled sponsored supplement and a graduated set of practical access and response rights. Editorial decisions remain with Vellumstone.”\nRelationship context: Valeria Falconer told Lars Hutchins informally that we would make Tanneryside “comfortable with” competitor copy. No written commitment was made. Acknowledge the intent to engage, but state that it did not create copy approval or a competitor veto and cannot displace our standards.\nConcession ladder (offer only in this order)\nStage\nPermitted offer and guardrails\n1  Bespoke data cut\nOffer first. A bounded subject, population and period agreed in the brief; aggregated/non-identifying output only. Methodology and limitations stay visible, and data is distinguished from Tanneryside interpretation. Incremental cost: £6,000. Projected contribution: £162,000.\n2  Logo placement\nDesignated sponsorship furniture or promotional positions only, with a prominent “Sponsored supplement”/“Advertisement feature” disclosure. The logo must not imply authorship or endorsement of independent copy. No separately measurable monetary effect supplied.\n3  Advance sight (visibility, not approval)\nDefine the term before using it: pre-publication visibility for named, authorised Tanneryside recipients during a two-business-day review window. It confers no approval, veto, withdrawal or publication-decision right. Comments are limited to possible factual errors; Vellumstone verifies independently and decides any correction. PDF marked “Advance sight – version [ID] – confidential/embargoed”; no redistribution or public use. Later editorial changes do not trigger a fresh approval round. One Vellumstone editorial contact receives comments; no direct routing to writers, designers or production.\n4  Same-issue right of reply\nFallback only after the first three stages. Triggered by a material statement about Tanneryside or its products—not by a competitor mention or favourable treatment. Maximum half a page in the same issue; copy due by the production deadline. Vellumstone may edit, fact-check, label or decline material that is inaccurate, unlawful, over-promotional or otherwise unfit. Displaced advertising effect: £10,000. Projected contribution: £158,000; with data cut: £152,000.\nNon-negotiables and operating controls\nCopy approval is outside our negotiable authority. Tanneryside may not approve, require changes to, or delay copy.\nA right to pull, suppress or veto coverage because it names competing equipment is outside our negotiable authority. Competitor coverage is governed by relevance, evidence, accuracy and fair opportunity to address material criticism—not sponsor preference.\nFinal control stays with Vellumstone’s editorial team: commissioning, wording, headlines, images, prominence and publication. Product-performance claims need ordinary substantiation and editorial review; sponsorship does not allow insertion, removal or alteration on demand.\nKeep sponsored material visually and editorially distinct from independent coverage, with a prominent, readily understood disclosure on the supplement and any sponsorship furniture.\nCommercial negotiation sits with the publisher/commercial channel; editorial decisions sit with the editorial lead. Escalate any request beyond this note to Milena Bonneau before agreeing it. Meeting concessions are provisional until recorded in writing.\nAny agreed concession is for this supplement/issue only, creates no automatic renewal or other-title precedent, and does not replace Vellumstone’s ordinary post-publication corrections or complaints process.\nIf pressed for approval or competitor removal\nUse: “That request exceeds the available position. We can offer bounded factual review and, where the trigger is met, a half-page same-issue reply under editorial control. Approval or competitor-based removal cannot be agreed as framed; I will escalate any revised proposal to Milena before commitment.”\nFinancial note: contributions above are projections under the stated assumptions (sponsorship revenue less direct production cost and only the supplied incremental effects); they are not guaranteed profit, cash or a complete publishing margin.","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"R01","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Both required deliverables exist at the top level under the exact requested filenames and are valid, readable Office files.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":true,"evidence":"Working-directory file listing and successful parsing of both files.","grader_hint":"Confirm the exact names sponsorship_meeting_position.docx and concession_register.xlsx, then open or parse each file."},{"rubric_item_id":"R02","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The rendered position note is no more than four pages.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered DOCX page count.","grader_hint":"Render the DOCX using a standard office renderer and count all pages, including mostly blank trailing pages."},{"rubric_item_id":"R03","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook contains exactly one visible working worksheet and no more than twelve substantive concession rows.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Workbook structure and populated row inspection.","grader_hint":"Ignore a header row when counting concession rows; hidden worksheets still violate the one-worksheet constraint."},{"rubric_item_id":"R04","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The note identifies Thursday’s Tanneryside sponsorship meeting, Milena Bonneau as the meeting user, and the proposed twelve-page supplement.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Position-note opening or context statement.","grader_hint":"Accept equivalent concise wording, but all three contextual facts must be present."},{"rubric_item_id":"R05","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The note states that its practice and compliance frame is the UK as at 1 February 2025.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scope, basis or status wording in the note.","grader_hint":"Look for both the jurisdiction and date, not merely a generic reference to current rules."},{"rubric_item_id":"R06","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The note records an operational negotiating position rather than recommending whether Vellumstone should accept or reject the sponsorship overall.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Purpose, conclusion and overall framing of the note.","grader_hint":"Award when the document equips Milena with defined offers and limits but does not turn into an accept/reject recommendation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R07","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Before relying on the phrase, the note defines “advance sight” as pre-publication visibility that does not confer approval, veto, withdrawal or publication-decision rights.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Definitions or advance-sight provision.","grader_hint":"The definition must resolve the two competing readings rather than merely repeat the phrase."},{"rubric_item_id":"R08","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The note distinguishes factual-error notification from editorial approval and permits corrections only after editorial verification.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Advance-review or corrections language.","grader_hint":"Look for both elements: the sponsor may flag factual errors, and Vellumstone independently verifies and decides any change."},{"rubric_item_id":"R09","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The position expressly retains final control over commissioning, wording, headlines, images, prominence and publication with Vellumstone’s editorial team.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Editorial-control provision.","grader_hint":"Equivalent grouped language is acceptable if it clearly covers content and presentation decisions."},{"rubric_item_id":"R10","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Copy approval is identified as outside the negotiable authority rather than being offered as a concession.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Red-line or non-negotiable provision in either artifact.","grader_hint":"The position must clearly withhold approval rights; vague language about preserving independence is insufficient."},{"rubric_item_id":"R11","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The proposed right to pull, suppress or veto coverage because it names competing equipment is identified as outside the negotiable authority.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Red-line or competitor-coverage provision.","grader_hint":"The document must address the specific competitor-based kill right, not only a generic veto."},{"rubric_item_id":"R12","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The informal “comfortable with” promise is acknowledged accurately as relationship context, while the position clarifies that it did not create copy approval or a competitor veto.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Background, talking point or treatment of Valeria Falconer’s statement.","grader_hint":"Award when the note avoids both ignoring the promise and overstating it as a binding editorial commitment."},{"rubric_item_id":"R13","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The concession sequence begins with the bespoke data cut before any concession involving the appearance or handling of editorial copy.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":false,"evidence":"Ordered position in the note and sequence field in the register.","grader_hint":"Inspect the explicit order, not the accidental order in which topics happen to appear."},{"rubric_item_id":"R14","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Logo placement follows the bespoke data cut and precedes advance sight in the concession sequence.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":false,"evidence":"Ordered concession ladder in both deliverables.","grader_hint":"Both relationships must hold: data cut before logo, and logo before advance sight."},{"rubric_item_id":"R15","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Advance sight without approval precedes the same-issue right of reply in the concession sequence.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":false,"evidence":"Ordered concession ladder in both deliverables.","grader_hint":"The advance-sight stage must carry the no-approval qualification."},{"rubric_item_id":"R16","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Copy approval and the competitor-based kill right are kept outside the offer ladder and are not represented as later concessions.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":false,"evidence":"Sequence and status treatment in the note and register.","grader_hint":"They may appear as red lines or requested rights, but must not receive offer sequence numbers."},{"rubric_item_id":"R17","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The bespoke data-cut offer defines a bounded subject, population or period rather than promising unrestricted analysis.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Conditions attached to the data-cut concession.","grader_hint":"Accept any practical bounded scope; no particular invented dataset is required."},{"rubric_item_id":"R18","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The data-cut provision states that methodology, limitations and the distinction between data and sponsor interpretation remain visible.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Data-cut conditions or editorial-use caveat.","grader_hint":"Look for transparent methodological context and protection against sponsor-led reinterpretation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R19","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The data-cut provision limits output to suitably aggregated or non-identifying information and does not promise disclosure of confidential source data.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Data handling or confidentiality condition.","grader_hint":"Equivalent privacy-preserving language earns credit."},{"rubric_item_id":"R20","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Logo placement is confined to clearly identified sponsorship furniture or designated promotional positions and is not allowed to imply authorship of independent copy.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Logo-placement conditions.","grader_hint":"The boundary must address both location and misleading association with editorial authorship."},{"rubric_item_id":"R21","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The supplement is required to carry a prominent, readily understood sponsorship or advertising disclosure.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Labelling or transparency provision.","grader_hint":"Accept labels such as sponsored supplement, advertisement feature or advertorial when the wording is unambiguous and prominent."},{"rubric_item_id":"R22","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The position preserves a clear visual and editorial distinction between sponsored material and ordinary independent coverage.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Design, labelling and presentation safeguards considered together.","grader_hint":"Assess whether a reasonable reader would be unlikely to mistake sponsor-controlled promotion for ordinary editorial coverage."},{"rubric_item_id":"R23","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Advance-copy access is limited to named or authorised Tanneryside recipients for a defined review window.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Advance-sight operating conditions.","grader_hint":"A specific duration may be chosen by the author; award if the recipient class and a concrete deadline or window are stated."},{"rubric_item_id":"R24","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Advance copies are treated as confidential or embargoed and cannot be redistributed or used publicly before publication.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Advance-sight confidentiality condition.","grader_hint":"Look for a meaningful restriction on onward circulation or premature use."},{"rubric_item_id":"R25","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The advance-sight process identifies the reviewed version and makes clear that later editorial changes do not create a fresh approval round.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Version-control or copy-freeze language.","grader_hint":"Award for a practical version identifier, watermark or equivalent control plus closure of repeated review."},{"rubric_item_id":"R26","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Sponsor comments are routed through one identified Vellumstone editorial contact rather than directly to writers, designers or production staff.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Communication-channel provision.","grader_hint":"A role is sufficient; no invented person is required."},{"rubric_item_id":"R27","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The right of reply is triggered by a material statement about Tanneryside or its products, not by the mere mention or favourable treatment of a competitor.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Right-of-reply eligibility condition.","grader_hint":"The trigger must be narrower than general dissatisfaction with competitor coverage."},{"rubric_item_id":"R28","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The right of reply is expressly for the same issue and includes a submission deadline compatible with production.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Right-of-reply timing provision.","grader_hint":"Award only if both same-issue placement and an operational deadline are clear."},{"rubric_item_id":"R29","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The right-of-reply offer is capped at half a page and does not expand into a general entitlement to additional sponsored space.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Right-of-reply size and scope condition.","grader_hint":"The half-page cap comes from the supplied financial assumption and must be explicit."},{"rubric_item_id":"R30","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Vellumstone retains the right to edit, fact-check, label or decline reply material that is inaccurate, unlawful, promotional beyond scope or otherwise unfit to publish.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Editorial conditions on the right of reply.","grader_hint":"Equivalent concise fitness and verification criteria are acceptable."},{"rubric_item_id":"R31","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Competitor coverage is governed by relevance, evidence, accuracy and fair opportunity to address material criticism rather than sponsor preference.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Competitor-coverage standard.","grader_hint":"The standard should permit legitimate competitor coverage while imposing normal editorial fairness."},{"rubric_item_id":"R32","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Commercial sponsorship does not permit Tanneryside to insert, remove or alter product-performance claims without ordinary substantiation and editorial review.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Claims, fact-checking or sponsor-input provision.","grader_hint":"Look for evidence-based treatment of product claims, not simply a broad independence slogan."},{"rubric_item_id":"R33","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The position preserves Vellumstone’s ordinary post-publication corrections or complaints process for genuine errors.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Post-publication provision.","grader_hint":"The sponsor should retain an ordinary route to raise errors without receiving special removal rights."},{"rubric_item_id":"R34","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Commercial negotiation and editorial decisions are assigned to distinct accountable roles or channels.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Responsibilities or authority language.","grader_hint":"Award when the note prevents sales or sponsor contacts from directly making editorial decisions."},{"rubric_item_id":"R35","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Any request beyond the documented position must be escalated to a named Vellumstone role before it is agreed.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Authority or escalation provision.","grader_hint":"A role such as publisher or editor-in-chief is sufficient; the route must precede commitment."},{"rubric_item_id":"R36","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Meeting concessions are provisional until recorded in writing, preventing an unrecorded oral exchange from expanding the sponsor’s rights.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Recording or confirmation provision.","grader_hint":"Look for written confirmation or an equivalent contemporaneous control."},{"rubric_item_id":"R37","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Any agreed concessions are limited to this supplement or issue and do not automatically set terms for renewals or other titles.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Duration, precedent or renewal provision.","grader_hint":"The wording must address both finite scope and non-precedent."},{"rubric_item_id":"R38","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The note supplies a clear response if Tanneryside insists on approval or competitor-removal rights: the request exceeds the available position and requires escalation or cannot be agreed as framed.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Counter-response or boundary language.","grader_hint":"This should be usable in the room without becoming a recommendation on the overall sponsorship."},{"rubric_item_id":"R39","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Both deliverables use the supplied baseline figures of £240,000 sponsorship revenue, £72,000 direct production cost and twelve pages.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":false,"evidence":"Financial summary in the note and assumptions or scenario entries in the workbook.","grader_hint":"Compare the values and units across both files."},{"rubric_item_id":"R40","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The projected baseline contribution equals sponsorship revenue minus direct production cost: £168,000, with a tolerance of ±£1.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":false,"evidence":"Baseline scenario in both deliverables.","grader_hint":"Verify 240,000 minus 72,000 and confirm the result is not presented as revenue."},{"rubric_item_id":"R41","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The data-cut scenario includes the supplied £6,000 incremental cost and projects contribution of £162,000, with a tolerance of ±£1.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":false,"evidence":"Data-cut financial outcome in both deliverables.","grader_hint":"Verify 240,000 minus 72,000 minus 6,000."},{"rubric_item_id":"R42","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The half-page right-of-reply scenario includes the supplied £10,000 displaced-advertising effect and projects contribution of £158,000, with a tolerance of ±£1.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":false,"evidence":"Right-of-reply financial outcome in both deliverables.","grader_hint":"Verify 240,000 minus 72,000 minus 10,000."},{"rubric_item_id":"R43","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The combined data-cut and half-page reply scenario projects contribution of £152,000, with a tolerance of ±£1.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":false,"evidence":"Combined-concessions scenario in both deliverables.","grader_hint":"Verify 240,000 minus 72,000 minus 6,000 minus 10,000."},{"rubric_item_id":"R44","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Logo placement and advance sight carry no invented monetary effect, while their non-financial conditions remain visible.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":false,"evidence":"Financial-effect and conditions fields in the register, plus treatment in the note.","grader_hint":"Zero or 'no separately measurable cost supplied' is acceptable; do not accept an invented fee, saving or cost."},{"rubric_item_id":"R45","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Financial outcomes are labelled as projections under the stated assumptions rather than guaranteed profit, cash or final margin.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Financial-summary labels and assumption notes.","grader_hint":"The terminology should reflect that only revenue and specified direct effects were provided."},{"rubric_item_id":"R46","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook stores monetary inputs as numeric values and derives scenario contributions with formulas rather than typing every outcome as static text.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Cell types and formula inspection.","grader_hint":"At minimum, the four projected contribution outcomes should be formula-derived from visible numeric assumptions."},{"rubric_item_id":"R47","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Each substantive register entry makes its status and negotiating use clear through fields covering the offer or request, sequence or red-line status, conditions, authority or owner, and financial effect.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Workbook headers and populated concession rows.","grader_hint":"Equivalent headings are acceptable; judge whether Milena can distinguish what may be offered, under what conditions and by whom."},{"rubric_item_id":"R48","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook separately records all six material topics: bespoke data cut, logo placement, advance sight, right of reply, copy approval and competitor-based withdrawal or veto.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Concession-register rows.","grader_hint":"Synonyms are acceptable, but none of the six topics may be merged so completely that its individual status is unclear."},{"rubric_item_id":"R49","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The term “advance sight” has the same defined meaning in both files.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":false,"evidence":"Definition in the note and conditions or notes in the register.","grader_hint":"Both must preserve visibility without approval, veto or publication control."},{"rubric_item_id":"R50","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The sequence numbers and red-line statuses in the register reproduce the position note without contradiction.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":false,"evidence":"Comparison of the ordered ladder and boundaries across both files.","grader_hint":"Check all concession stages, not merely the first and last."},{"rubric_item_id":"R51","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Milena can navigate the note during a live meeting and determine the current offer, fallback, conditions and boundary without asking the author a clarifying question.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Overall structure, signposting, density and operational specificity of the note.","grader_hint":"Judge real-time usability rather than visual polish alone."},{"rubric_item_id":"R52","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The two artifacts are professionally written, editable and reusable as an internal record, with concise labels, legible presentation and no material contradiction or unsupported legal certainty.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":false,"evidence":"Overall inspection of both deliverables.","grader_hint":"Allow reasonable house style variation; withhold credit for a polished but ambiguous or operationally unusable package."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"Vellumstone Press is managing a commercially important supplement proposal whose requested sponsor controls conflict with ordinary editorial safeguards. The documents will be used by the publisher during a live negotiation and retained as the record of the permitted negotiating position.","difficulty_sources":["Defining an ambiguous sponsor-facing term before using it operationally","Reconciling an informal commercial promise with editorial independence","Sequencing bounded concessions without turning approval or suppression rights into negotiable defaults","Maintaining numerical and semantic agreement between a prose note and an editable register"],"authoring_plan":{"mode_and_intent":"Construct a normative internal position that records permitted negotiating conduct rather than recommending whether to accept the sponsorship. The professional challenge is to preserve editorial independence while leaving a commercially usable concession path.","reference_material":"No reference files are created. All arbitrary local facts needed for scoring, including filenames, parties, date, page count, financial assumptions and required topics, are carried in the request.","gold_relationships":["The offer sequence is bespoke data cut, then bounded logo placement, then advance sight without approval, then a conditional same-issue right of reply.","Copy approval and any right to pull or suppress coverage because it names competitors are red lines outside the numbered offer sequence.","Advance sight means pre-publication visibility for bounded factual comments; it never means approval, veto, withdrawal authority or final publication control.","The informal promise to keep Tanneryside comfortable is acknowledged as relationship context but does not override editorial standards or create an approval right.","Baseline projected contribution is sponsorship revenue less direct production cost.","The data-cut scenario deducts the supplied incremental data cost from baseline contribution.","The right-of-reply scenario deducts the supplied displaced-advertising amount from baseline contribution.","The combined scenario deducts both supplied incremental effects.","Logo placement and advance sight have no separately measurable monetary effect because the request supplies none.","All financial outcomes are projections under limited assumptions, not guaranteed profit or a complete publishing P&L."],"required_professional_content":["Clear sponsored-content labelling and visible separation from independent editorial material.","Final editorial control over commissioning, wording, presentation and publication.","A bounded factual-correction channel that does not become approval.","Confidential, controlled and version-specific handling of advance copy.","A right-of-reply trigger tied to material statements about Tanneryside, with a half-page cap, same-issue timing, production deadline and editorial fitness review.","Competitor coverage governed by relevance, evidence, accuracy and fairness rather than sponsor preference.","A bounded data-cut scope with methodology and privacy safeguards.","Distinct commercial and editorial authority, escalation beyond mandate and written confirmation of any concession.","Issue-specific duration and explicit non-precedent treatment for renewals.","An in-room response for demands that exceed the position."],"workbook_behaviour":"Create one editable worksheet with visible numeric assumptions and formula-derived scenario contributions. Each material topic receives a distinguishable row or entry with offer/request, order or red-line status, conditions, authority and financial effect. Keep the populated concession entries within the twelve-row cap.","document_behaviour":"Create a concise position note that can be scanned during a live meeting, defines the ambiguous term before operational use, records the promise without inflating it, and keeps factual position-setting distinct from an overall sponsorship recommendation.","cross_deliverable_controls":"Use identical monetary figures, scenario outcomes, concession order, status labels and meaning of advance sight in both files. The workbook should function as the structured control record for the prose position.","intended_verdict":"A passing solution gives Milena a commercially graduated but editorially bounded position, uses the supplied assumptions exactly, makes the two files agree and remains usable without author clarification. A plausible-looking submission that offers approval, permits competitor suppression, leaves advance sight ambiguous, ignores the informal promise or invents financial effects should lose the associated credit."},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"mixed_media_bundle","structure":"supplied_template"},"reference_files":[],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"position_note","filename":"sponsorship_meeting_position.docx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","description":"A concise negotiating position note for the publisher’s sponsorship meeting.","required":true,"constraints":["Maximum four rendered pages; must state operational boundaries without recommending whether to accept the sponsorship overall; must use only the monetary assumptions supplied in the request."],"rendering_required":true},{"deliverable_id":"concession_register","filename":"concession_register.xlsx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet","description":"An editable register of concession sequence, conditions, boundaries and projected financial outcomes.","required":true,"constraints":["One worksheet and no more than twelve concession rows; calculations, terminology and sequencing must agree with the position note."],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"document_information","work_product":"professional_report","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"closed_world_with_assumptions"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"authored_doc@v4","occupation":"editors","sector":"information","task_archetype":"authored_doc","estimated_professional_hours":4.0,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"hybrid","reviewer_policy":"A domain-expert editorial reviewer checks the position for sponsorship labelling, editorial independence, fair-treatment and negotiation-governance norms. An independent spreadsheet reviewer verifies formulas, scenario arithmetic, file constraints and cross-deliverable consistency.","minimum_reviewers":2,"known_limitations":["The task does not require a definitive legal opinion or verbatim citation of a particular industry code. Operational time windows and role labels may vary if they are explicit, internally coherent and consistent across the two deliverables."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"结构/材料验收记录","detail":"validated 属于结构、防泄漏、材料推进验收；没有内容正确率结论。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-24T21:29:36+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-24T21:29:36+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-24T21:29:36+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-24T21:29:36+00:00"},{"check":"instruction_rubric_overlap","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":false,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-24T21:29:36+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_c2/runs/fa52069a7138eeb0","declared_deliverables":["sponsorship_meeting_position.docx","concession_register.xlsx"]};
